a overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295580721\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Both web transports inject EVERY request field into a command's params as nn_<key> — nn_sessionid is just the one the author-defaulting uses; nn_session (the whole session object), headers-derived fields, etc. are equally available to any command that declares them.\",\n    \"detail\": \"HTTP: app/exec puts nn_sessionid into args after check_auth; websocket: the cmd handler copies all request fields as nn_* into params before dispatch (app/service/init.rs). Declared params are REQUIRED by the generated wrapper, so a command declaring nn_* still works on the web (injected) but CLI/MCP callers must pass it explicitly (\\\"\\\").\",\n    \"tags\": \"frontend,bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786411233530\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"flowlang Command::cast_params (0.3.31, command.rs:158) panics on a MALFORMED value for a declared Integer param - parse::<i64>().unwrap() - killing the HTTP handler thread; the 0.3.30 wrapper guard covers only MISSING params. Any UI that builds command URLs from unvalidated DOM values (empty select -> width=, undefined chains, Date arithmetic -> NaN) can panic a thread per request; a retrying poller makes it continuous, which is how the owner hit it in the camera settings preview (2026-08-11). Until fixed upstream, the library-side idiom is: declare URL-facing numeric params as String and parse leniently in-body with a soft-fail (camera does this across snapshot/keyframe/events_page since 228b089); declared-type changes are wire-compatible because query params are strings anyway.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,cast_params,panic,http,params,hardening\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"owner panic report + disposable repro, flowlang 0.3.31 command.rs:158, 2026-08-11\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786472610314\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The generated cmd crate de